  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nAs per current spec, the custom registry for new elements is taken from the \"intended parent\", which is initialized when initializing the fragment parser inert document.\n\nFor the template case, this initialized from the template's custom element registry.\nHowever, no browser implements this - in both webkit/blink which currently implement custom element registry, the registry in this case is null.\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12624 changes the specified behavior to match implementations (with corresponding tests), as this behavior seems to affect some other tests due to subtle timing issues.\n\nWe should decide what the desired behavior is here and fix the spec together with implementation+tests if this is different from what's currently tested+implemented.\n\n\n\n\n",
